7. The points that arise for my consideration are;
1. Whether the prosecution proves beyond all reasonable doubt that, the accused No.1 was married with CW.1 on 17.11.2019 and thereafter, the accused No.1 to 3 in furtherance of common intention have subjected CW.1 to cruelty by harassing her both by physically and mentally for dowry and thereby committed an offence punishable U/s.498A R/ w. Sec.34 of IPC ?
C.C.No.51090/2022 2.

opennyai_summary.decision:
12. Point No.3 :- In view of the findings on above points, I proceed to pass the following;
C.C.No.51090/2022 ORDER Acting under section 248(1) of Cr.P.C. the accused No.1 to 3 are acquitted of the offence punishable under Secs.498A R/w Sec.34 of IPC and Secs.3 and 4 of D.P.Act.
The bail bonds of the accused No.1 to 3 shall be in force for the period of 6 months and thereafter it shall be cancelled without further orders.

